    "title": "Compare inferiority and perspectives",
    "subtitle": "Learn, understand, and use a Mandarin pattern.",
    "context": "Use the introduced pattern in a bounded sentence. Other wording may be valid Chinese; this task checks this pattern and these words.",
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "EX-GRAM-G-hsk4-comparison-teach",
        "kind": "teach",
        "title": "Compare inferiority and perspectives",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "text": "不如 directly expresses inferiority. A negative 比 sentence merely denies superiority. 跟…相比 sets an explicit comparison perspective.",
            "examples": [
              {
                "text": "我不如他高。",
                "pinyin": "wǒ bùrú tā gāo 。",
                "meaning": "I am not as tall as he is.",
                "audio": "1e513e996d37347c55b34e5aade8a8e98176fc3e2288f0877ef59277f60feac4"
              },
              {
                "text": "我不比他高。",
                "pinyin": "wǒ bù bǐ tā gāo 。",
                "meaning": "I am not taller than he is.",
                "audio": "7018fd3b32dcb93217fc190b97502b0bde662088dc90c2a1b13fc00f20d54239"
              },
              {
                "text": "跟他相比，我比较忙。",
                "pinyin": "gēn tā xiāngbǐ ， wǒ bǐjiào máng 。",
                "meaning": "Compared with him, I am rather busy.",
                "audio": "59f464f0f8af5f8f63c3462759563caf70e0fd97e99e1b7fee8534fb1df5f6af"
              }
            ]
          },
